  {
    "id": "29100c5c-42de-5523-9629-bb38e7887e75",
    "pack": "bestiary-2",
    "kind": "action",
    "slug": "action:vampire-vrykolakas-vrykolakas-vulnerabilities",
    "name": "(Vampire, Vrykolakas) Vrykolakas Vulnerabilities",
    "rarity": "common",
    "traits": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "bestiary-2"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Vrykolakas all have the following vulnerabilities."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
          [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Burial Site Bound",
                  "marks": ["strong"]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " A vrykolakas is bound to the place of its death or interment. It must return to this location once per week and bury itself in the earth for 24 hours, during which time it is "
                },
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "id": "7802f1d9-5ced-5b9b-8a08-98ec0adb9947"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " and can be beheaded. If it is unable to return to this site, it is reduced to 0 Hit Points and attempts to use Feral Corruption; if this host animal can't return to the burial site before the possession effect ends, the vrykolakas is destroyed and the animal host returns to normal."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Vulnerable to Decapitation",
                  "marks": ["strong"]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " A vrykolakas that is beheaded can't use its Feral Possession, and a beheaded corpse cannot rise as a vrykolakas."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.5arYoSY5kcRo8TeM"
    },
    "data": {
      "category": "defensive"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "e02659d2-6f97-5c9a-95bf-74af7c74421a",
    "pack": "bestiary-2",
    "kind": "action",
    "slug": "action:worm-that-walks-discorporate",
    "name": "(Worm That Walks) Discorporate",
    "rarity": "common",
    "traits": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "bestiary-2"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "When the worm that walks is reduced to 0 HP, it discorporates and the component worms that make up its body disperse in every direction. If even a single worm escapes, the worm that walks will eventually re-form using a process that typically takes 1d10 days."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "While the exact circumstances and surroundings determine how long the worm that walks's foes have to dispatch the fleeing worms before they escape, usually its foes have only a single round."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Typically, this requires the application of an area effect or splash weapon within 1 round to the space where the worm that walks collapsed. After any amount of area or splash damage is dealt to that space, the character dealing the damage must attempt a "
          },
          {
            "type": "check",
            "statistic": "flat",
            "dc": 15
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " check. Each subsequent area or splash damage effect performed on the area reduces the DC of this flat check by 2, to a minimum of DC 5. If any of these flat checks succeed, none of the worms escape, and the worm that walks is destroyed permanently."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "At the GM's discretion, clever means of trapping or otherwise detaining the vermin may extend the time allowed to finish off the worm that walks."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.QlrbnkeZu6M4kvOy"
    },
    "data": {
      "category": "defensive"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "b926e650-9bcb-5608-98e2-54023a6d9f1b",
    "pack": "bestiary-2",
    "kind": "action",
    "slug": "action:worm-that-walks-squirming-embrace",
    "name": "(Worm That Walks) Squirming Embrace",
    "rarity": "common",
    "traits": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "bestiary-2"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The worm that walks Strides, ending its movement sharing a space with a creature, and deals piercing damage to the creature equal to "
          },
          {
            "type": "damage",
            "instances": [
              {
                "formula": "1d8",
                "damageType": "piercing"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " plus an additional 1d8 for every 3 levels the worm that walks has. The creature can attempt a "
          },
          {
            "type": "check",
            "statistic": "save:reflex",
            "basic": true
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " save with a DC of the worm that walks's spell DC - 2."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.Zu6feO9NUZJlsKuc"
    },
    "data": {
      "cost": "one",
      "category": "offensive"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "9f7fb8e9-ca81-5a1f-b395-e0ccfa4e8d37",
    "pack": "bestiary-2",
    "kind": "action",
    "slug": "action:worm-that-walks-swarm-shape",
    "name": "(Worm That Walks) Swarm Shape",
    "rarity": "common",
    "traits": ["concentrate"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "bestiary-2"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The worm that walks collapses into a shapeless swarm of worms. It drops all held, worn, and carried items."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "While discorporated, the worm that walks can't use attack actions and can't cast spells, but it can move through areas small enough for its individual worms to fit without having to Squeeze. It can use the same action to coalesce back into its normal form."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-family-ability-glossary.Item.X2mdpb1Dhl890YbA"
    },
    "data": {
      "cost": "one",
      "category": "offensive"
    }
  }
]
